    inc=['Form 16 and salary review', 'AIS and Form 26AS reconciliation', 'Old vs new regime comparison', 'Deductions and exemptions', 'Interest, rent and other income', 'Filing and e-verification', 'Refund tracking'],
    g='No government fee. Late filing fees apply after the due date.',
    d=ITR_BASE + [('Form 16', 'From each employer during the year.'), ('Investment and deduction proofs', 'If you use the old regime.'), ('Rent receipts', 'For HRA, under the old regime.'), ('Home loan certificate', 'If you have one.')],
    s=ITR_STEPS,
    f=[('Which ITR form should I file?', 'ITR-1 if you are a resident with salary, one house property and other income up to ₹50 lakh. Otherwise, usually ITR-2.'),
       ('New regime or old regime?', 'The new regime is the default and has lower rates but few deductions. The old regime can be better if you claim large deductions. We compare both for you.'),
       ('What is the due date?', '31 July for ITR-1 and ITR-2 filers, unless extended.'),
       ('What if I changed jobs during the year?', 'Combine income and TDS from all employers. Missing a Form 16 is a common reason for notices.')],
